4. Press **Save as checked**, then **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/admin-21-tolls-review-desktop-c59d0a1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1150; address: carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read/76f10bea-9140-487b-89c8-a5cc8f15b59b; pins: 1 42.6 16.8, 2 56.7 43.8, 3 90.3 60.9, 4 76.0 38.0")

> Tip: Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and the administration fee, when "Charge renters matched with high confidence now" is ticked. Other lines go to the work queue or stay as exceptions with the reason.


## Deposit reviews before a release

Every returned booking with a deposit is reviewed twice before any of the deposit is released: Fleet signs fuel, kilometres, damage, late return, cleaning, tickets and highway tolls against the pickup photos, then Finance double-checks each, checks the toll operator and every ticket place. **Money** > **Payments** > **Deposit reviews** lists them; each booking has a **Deposit review** card. You may sign either side. To release a deposit before the review is done, use the settlement on the booking''s **Money** with the reason; it is recorded.

**Settings** > **Program settings**: **Deposit review required** (on), **Deposit review sweep days** (mon,wed,fri), **Deposit review toll url**, and **Deposit review ticket places**: each place''s name and official lookup link, edited as a list. A place you add applies to the reviews made after the change. **Money** > **Payments** > **Countdowns** shows the time left on every deposit hold, deposit return and plan payment, soonest first.

The accident card of a booking with the plan sold with the rental shows the renter''s own policy number and the provider''s claim page (Program settings, accident plan claim url). When the number was not captured at purchase, enter it on the booking''s accident card with **Enter the plan policy number**.

## 407 ETR statements

1. Read the statement PDF or its CSV download (the PDF and the CSV of one statement are the same trips: read one of them).
2. Each trip is read from its column: the date and the entry time, the plate (from its own column, or the Licence Plate line above its trips), the entry and the exit, and the toll with its camera and trip toll charges. The line''s amount is what the renter owes for the trip; Of which fees is the camera and trip toll charges. A distance is never read as money.
3. The monthly account fee and a late payment charge are not trips: they are listed under the read as left out.
4. A credit or a reversal is left out and said. A line whose charges do not add up to its total is marked for you to check.
5. Each trip goes to whoever had the car at that minute. Within the boundary margin of Program settings (30 minutes) of a rental''s start or end, a person confirms who had it; nothing is charged by itself there.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Toll notices and tickets arrive by mail and email. Read them into the system, check each line against the notice, and the matching, charges and emails follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-the-work-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The work queue</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter the queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged, Owner not billed, Staff, Charged not notified, Disputed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each toll shows its notice, kind, issuer, plate, when, amount and who it was matched to.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add one by one with <b class="gd-ui">Log one</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and match</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Import a CSV</b> takes a statement file.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/500"><img src="/guides/img/admin-19-tolls-desktop-baa198d0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="500"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.6%;top:32.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:59.7%;top:52%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.8%;top:21.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-inside-a-toll" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Inside a toll</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open a toll from the queue. Decide who pays: <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Bill to the owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars pays</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Wrong notice? Press <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b>. Finance can also press <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reading profiles (top right on Read a notice) teach the reader an issuer&#39;s layout. Paste a notice&#39;s text under &quot;Try it&quot; to test one.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="tolls-and-tickets-read-a-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo (JPEG or PNG) or a CSV, under 15 MB.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave Reading profile on finding it from the text, or choose the issuer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. The file is stored first, then read in your browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Notices read lists every read with its status and counts.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-20-tolls-read-desktop-d733b5f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:41.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.1%;top:52.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin