- **Coverage**: no card picked, a card that does not cover this car, or a box not ticked.
- **Limits**: 3 requests already open for that person, or more than 30 requests in an hour from one internet connection.
- **Our system could not take the request**: the customer is told we kept the request and will contact them. The To-do is urgent and shows what the system said. Tell the developer if you see the same one twice.

> Good to know: An add-on that cannot be added online never stops a request. The request arrives without the add-ons and its note starts with "Add-ons asked for, not added online": confirm them with the renter in the offer.

## Show a lead''s phone to a salesperson (release 46)

Sales see customer numbers with most digits hidden. To give one salesperson the full number of one lead:

1. On the lead (its page, its card, or its row under Expired offers on the Leads tab of Renters), press **Show the phone to** and the salesperson''s name: the lead''s salesperson, or the person holding its claim. On the lead''s page you can choose another Sales person and type a reason.
2. That person gets an alert that opens the lead, and now sees the full number on that lead only, with a call link and **Copy**. Every other lead stays hidden for them, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone), and nobody else gets it.
3. **Hide it again** beside their name hides it. Reassigning the lead hides it by itself: the new salesperson sees it only once you show it to them.
4. A salesperson can press **Ask an Admin to show the number**: you get a To do on the lead with **Show the phone**, which shows it to the one who asked and closes the To do.

> Good to know: each show and hide is in the audit log with who, when, for whom and the reason.

## Where a lead came from (release 48)

Every lead card and every lead''s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.

1. On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example "ChatGPT", "Google search", "Google Ads", "Perplexity", "Bing" or "Direct (typed or bookmarked)", with the search terms when we have them and "First page" (the first page they opened on the site).
2. On the lead''s page, the card **Where they came from** lists: **Came from**, **Search terms**, **First page they opened**, **Page of the latest visit**, **Referring page** and **Campaign**. A row we do not know is left out.
3. Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.
4. Use it in the first call: someone who came from "kill switch for car" wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.

> Good to know: a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.

## Duplicate leads

The same person often writes twice: the contact form, then the chat, then a call. Leads joins them by itself.

1. Two open leads of the same kind join when they have the same email or the same phone and the names fit (the same last name, the same first initial, or one has no name). A name alone joins only with the same city or the same car asked about, within 30 days; otherwise it is offered as a possible duplicate.
2. The lead someone is working on is kept: a live claim, a logged contact, an assigned salesperson, a stage past New or a lead generator. The other''s message, calls, texts, chats and notes move to it, under "Also wrote". Nothing is deleted.
3. A new enquiry from someone whose lead was handled joins that lead and makes it New again, with the same salesperson, who gets an alert.
4. When both leads are being worked on, they are not joined: the card shows "possible duplicate: merge" and you choose. **Merge** keeps the oldest; **Different person** stops the suggestion.
5. A renter lead and an owner lead of the same person stay apart: they are different conversations.

> Good to know: the check runs when a lead arrives or its name, email or phone changes, and every hour. Every merge is in the audit log with the lead that was merged, so it can be traced.
## Duplicates merge by themselves, lead generators and call flags (release 50)

1. Open leads of one person and the same kind of customer merge by themselves, from any source and of any age: the same email, the same phone, or names written another way (the words in another order, a middle name or not) when their emails and phones do not disagree. The older lead is kept with everything from the other. Each merge is in the audit log and under the lead.
2. **Lead generators** (beside **Sales team**): press **Make someone a lead generator** for a salesperson who finds car owners. They add owners on Owners I found; the closers call them through the site. When an owner they found signs, a credit of the amount in Program settings waits here: **Approve**, then **Mark paid** with the reference, or **Void** with the reason.
3. **Call flags** (beside **Sales team**): each line a salesperson said on a call with a phone number, swearing, a payment outside the site, a personal number, cash only, a threat or discrimination, and each text with a phone number they tried to send (not sent). Press **Mark reviewed** with a note. **Add a word** adds to the list; **Switch off** stops a word.
4. **Team** > **Shift claims**: a salesperson who works field shifts claims a shift here first. Press **Approve** to give it to them, or **Deny** with the reason. They are told either way.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b>. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead&#39;s own page.</p><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-what-is-in-the-list" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What is in the list</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Partner leads</b>: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-work-a-lead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a lead</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Claim</b> on a card, or <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or <b class="gd-ui">Note</b> adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Outcome</b> and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing more to do? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark handled</b>. Done with it for now? Press <b class="gd-ui">Unclaim</b>: it goes back to the pool at once.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead&#39;s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-as-an-admin" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">As an Admin</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> gives a lead to a person (their claim, and the lead is assigned to them). <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> ends someone&#39;s claim.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Sales team</b> shows each person&#39;s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-rebooking-intent-and-leads-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rebooking, intent and leads (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A returning renter&#39;s new request goes straight to the salesperson of their last booking, with the usual claim time.</li><li>Every renter and lead has an intent score (hot, warm or cold) with what they said they want: budget, car class, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage, read from calls (with their transcripts), texts, emails, the site chat and their visits.</li><li>Leads are never given out by themselves: onboarded Sales claim them, one every 5 minutes, up to 3 open at once plus one for every 5 won in the last 30 days (at most 10).</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-leads-handled-on-a-call-by-customer-service-or-fleet-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Leads handled on a call by customer service or Fleet (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">A lead that customer service or Fleet handle on a call (they answer or place the call, add a note, or create the lead from the call) is held for them for <b class="gd-ui">Customer service and Fleet: a lead they handle on a call is held for</b> minutes in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> (empty: the Sales claim minutes of its type). Each new handled call adds the time. Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> and cannot work it; <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it. <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> on the lead ends it at once; it returns to the salesperson who had a claim on it or brought it, else the open list. Your own reassign also ends it. A booking made from the lead keeps the usual credit; the hold is not a claim, so customer service is never credited. Every step is in the lead&#39;s history (hold, another call handled, hold ended).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-the-person-behind-the-lead-and-assigning-leads-in-bulk-relea" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The person behind the lead, and assigning leads in bulk (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The person.</b> Open a lead, or press <b class="gd-ui">The person</b> on its card, to see everything we know about whoever sent it, matched by their renter record, email and phone: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, whether they have an account and whether their licence is verified (yes or no; the number is never shown), every booking (car, dates, status, total and any open balance), what they owe and their deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, their messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents and claims, and who has handled them (Helped by, and who claimed, held or was assigned their leads).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Signals.</b> The intent score and the <b class="gd-ui">Signals</b> timeline are for the whole person, not one lead: calls (in, out, missed, with their length), texts both ways, WhatsApp, Messenger and Instagram messages, the site chat, emails they wrote, links they opened in our emails, visits and cars looked at, offers, quotes and payment pages opened, bookings, rentals, cancellations and reviews. Newest first.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Assign in bulk.</b> On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, tick cards (or <b class="gd-ui">Select all on this page</b>), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Everything the filter matches</b> to take every open lead the filters show (status, type, source, age, person, words). Choose a Sales person in <b class="gd-ui">Assign to</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Return to the pool</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Assign</b>: you see how many leads match and confirm first. <b class="gd-ui">Assign every unassigned lead older than today</b> takes every open lead nobody has (no person, no claim, no hold) that came in before today, after the same confirm. Up to 500 leads go per press; when more match, it says how many are left: press again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Only active, fully onboarded Sales staff can be chosen. Customer service, Fleet and Finance take no sales credit, so they are not in the list.</li><li>A bulk assignment is your assignment, not a claim: it does not run out, nobody else can claim the lead, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it for everyone else. The person&#39;s claims on their assigned leads do not count against their limits.</li><li>A customer service or Fleet call can still hold the lead while they handle it; when the hold ends, the lead goes back to the assigned person.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> on one lead still gives a timed claim, as before. <b class="gd-ui">Return to the pool</b> ends the assignment and any claim.</li><li>Every lead moved shows <b class="gd-ui">Assigned by an Admin to</b> in its history, and each press is one entry in the audit log.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-requests-that-did-not-go-through-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests that did not go through (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">When a customer presses <b class="gd-ui">Send request</b> and the request is refused or fails, nothing is lost. The form keeps everything they typed, tells them the exact reason beside the field to change, and Sales gets a To-do.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b> you see <b class="gd-ui">Requests that did not go through</b> with a count, when there is one. Open it for the reasons and the people: name, email, phone, the car, the dates, the reason they were shown, how many times they tried and when.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each person is listed once per car and day, however many times they tried. The newest reason is shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales has a <b class="gd-ui">Request did not go through</b> To-do for each one, with the same details. Call or text the person and help them finish, or make the offer yourself with <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When that person&#39;s request goes through, they leave the list and the To-do closes by itself.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The reasons a customer can see, and what each asks them to change:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Dates</b>: the pickup is too soon, the return is before the pickup, the booking is longer than one booking covers, or the car is taken or leaves the fleet first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Car</b>: the car cannot be booked online right now.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Place</b>: a delivery address or an airport is missing, or the car is not handed over at its owner&#39;s location.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Driver</b>: the email, the phone, the date of birth or the age for this car, the licence class, or an additional driver&#39;s details.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b>: no card picked, a card that does not cover this car, or a box not ticked.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Limits</b>: 3 requests already open for that person, or more than 30 requests in an hour from one internet connection.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Our system could not take the request</b>: the customer is told we kept the request and will contact them. The To-do is urgent and shows what the system said. Tell the developer if you see the same one twice.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An add-on that cannot be added online never stops a request. The request arrives without the add-ons and its note starts with &quot;Add-ons asked for, not added online&quot;: confirm them with the renter in the offer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-show-a-lead-s-phone-to-a-salesperson-release-46" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Show a lead&#39;s phone to a salesperson (release 46)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sales see customer numbers with most digits hidden. To give one salesperson the full number of one lead:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the lead (its page, its card, or its row under Expired offers on the Leads tab of Renters), press <b class="gd-ui">Show the phone to</b> and the salesperson&#39;s name: the lead&#39;s salesperson, or the person holding its claim. On the lead&#39;s page you can choose another Sales person and type a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">That person gets an alert that opens the lead, and now sees the full number on that lead only, with a call link and <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>. Every other lead stays hidden for them, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone), and nobody else gets it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide it again</b> beside their name hides it. Reassigning the lead hides it by itself: the new salesperson sees it only once you show it to them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A salesperson can press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to show the number</b>: you get a To do on the lead with <b class="gd-ui">Show the phone</b>, which shows it to the one who asked and closes the To do.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>each show and hide is in the audit log with who, when, for whom and the reason.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-where-a-lead-came-from-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where a lead came from (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every lead card and every lead&#39;s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example &quot;ChatGPT&quot;, &quot;Google search&quot;, &quot;Google Ads&quot;, &quot;Perplexity&quot;, &quot;Bing&quot; or &quot;Direct (typed or bookmarked)&quot;, with the search terms when we have them and &quot;First page&quot; (the first page they opened on the site).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the lead&#39;s page, the card <b class="gd-ui">Where they came from</b> lists: <b class="gd-ui">Came from</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Search terms</b>, <b class="gd-ui">First page they opened</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Page of the latest visit</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Referring page</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Campaign</b>. A row we do not know is left out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Use it in the first call: someone who came from &quot;kill switch for car&quot; wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-duplicate-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Duplicate leads</h2><p 