1. **Settings** > **Program settings** holds the timing: the reminder hours (1 and 3 days unless you change them), the hours before expiry for the last one (24, 0 for none) and the links allowed in all (3).
2. Every reminder is in the candidate''s emails, and the hiring job''s result counts the reminders sent, the texts and those held.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role&#39;s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.</p><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-open-a-role-and-send-the-apply-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Open a role and send the apply link</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the role</b> to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); <b class="gd-ui">Close the role</b> takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role&#39;s questions, about five minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pass mark and pay</b> changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-what-happens-to-each-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens to each application</h2><p class="gd-p">The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so. The email&#39;s button is <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>: one press makes their Sales application from the one they sent (no new form) and sends the AI interview link at once.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email (release 44: no start date in it; training and claiming shifts only, then a hello in the team chat and the member tag &quot;Name - Position&quot; in each WhatsApp group, also a first-day To do); their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line and the answer&#39;s score out of 10. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-redo-the-ai-interview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Redo the AI interview</h2><p class="gd-p">If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant&#39;s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Redo the AI interview</b>, then confirm.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Their staff access ends if they were already hired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The application goes back to <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b> and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-dates-before-the-townhall-release-35-widened-in-re" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 5:30 pm to 6:30 pm), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page. Interview call slots start at 5:30 pm Toronto time.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-the-sales-funnel-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Sales funnel (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Pipeline tab opens with <b class="gd-ui">Sales funnel</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sales staff in the academy</b>: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows &quot;Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago&quot;. A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The re-send</b>: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The bar for Sales</b>: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI&#39;s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-calls-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview calls in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">A video interview is now a private call inside the site, one room per slot, in place of the Jitsi link. The candidate&#39;s booking email (with a calendar invite) has their own link: it opens the call in their browser with no account, and works in one browser only (another browser is refused; a moved or cancelled call&#39;s link stops working). Opening the candidate yourself never uses their link: on the candidate&#39;s page press <b class="gd-ui">Join the interview call</b>. Their details, answers, the role&#39;s questions and the rubric are beside the video, with <b class="gd-ui">No show</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b>; Hire and the decision email stay on the candidate&#39;s page.</p><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a call in the site too (Townhall, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b>): you present, your slide is everyone&#39;s, and People shows who is in the call, who left and who has not joined. Attendance is recorded by itself. If the media server is down, <b class="gd-ui">Switch to the outside link</b> on the Townhall page sends everyone to the link in Program settings until you switch back.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-recruited-by-a-salesperson-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Recruited by a salesperson (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">In-person salespeople have an invite link to the in-person Sales application. A candidate who applies from it shows <b class="gd-ui">Recruited by</b> and the salesperson&#39;s name under Contact and source. Nothing is skipped: they are screened and interviewed like everyone. The salesperson is told when they apply and when they are hired.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-reminders-and-the-one-tap-new-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview reminders and the one-tap new link</h2><p class="gd-p">An invited candidate who has not sent their AI interview in gets a reminder with the one-tap link 1 day and 3 days after the link went, and the day before it expires. A text goes with it to a Canadian or US number while texts are on. No reminder goes while another email to them still waits to be sent, and none once the interview is in.</p><p class="gd-p">When a link has expired, the interview page offers <b class="gd-ui">Open a new link and start now</b>: one tap gives them a new link for the usual days and starts the interview, with no email needed. They can do this until they have had 3 links in all.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> holds the timing: the reminder hours (1 and 3 days unless you change them), the hours before expiry for the last one (24, 0 for none) and the links allowed in all (3).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every reminder is in the candidate&#39;s emails, and the hiring job&#39;s result counts the reminders sent, the texts and those held.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'admin-call', 'chapter', 'hiring', null, 'The weekly Admin call', 'The deck, the decisions to take, the call and its invite.',
  'The Admin call is the weekly call of the Admins (Team > Admin call). By default it is every Sunday at 7:00 pm Toronto time, for 60 minutes: change the day, the time or the length with **Change the day or time** on the page, or in Settings > Program settings (Admin call). Every Admin gets the weekly calendar invite by email (a calendar file: accept it once and it repeats), and an update when the time changes. **Add to my calendar (every week)** downloads the same event.

## The deck

The deck builds itself the day before the call and again three hours before, from the live data; **Build again** rebuilds it any time. An alert reaches the Admins an hour before. One slide a section:

1. Shifts for the coming week: what is published, the spots still open and each claim.
2. Staff hours (last 7 days) and the staff payouts owed.
3. Academy progress, person by person.
4. Hiring: new applications, interviews booked, waiting for a decision, hired, and the interview no-shows by first name.
5. Social media: the posts planned for the coming week, those still to approve, last week''s posts and figures.
6. The numbers of the last 7 days: bookings, revenue booked, occupancy, real visitors, conversion, leads by source and sales by rep.
7. Owners: applications, cars onboarding, statements to approve, payouts due, cars in arrears.
8. Deposits to release or keep.
9. Insurance billing and replacement rentals.
10. Claims.
11. Prepared money actions (from Claude).
12. Tolls and tickets.
13. Fleet: cars out of service, maintenance To dos, cars free all next week, cars missing photos.
14. To dos on the Admin queue that need a decision.

## Approve and Deny

Every decision is on its slide with its two buttons, decided once (the name of the Admin who pressed it shows):

- *A shift claim*: Approve keeps it; Take off the shift removes the person from it.
- **A To do**: Decline closes it with your reason; Approve leaves it open, marked approved.
- *A prepared money action*: Approve marks it approved and urgent; Decline closes it. No money moves from the deck: it moves only from its own screen.
- *A deposit* (Release or Keep) and *an owner payout* (Pay it or Hold it): the decision goes to Finance as a To do, done in Deposit reviews or Payouts with their usual checks.

Add a note to any slide. **Join the call** opens the call in the site, with the deck beside it; only Admins can join it.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The Admin call is the weekly call of the Admins (Team &gt; Admin call). By default it is every Sunday at 7:00 pm Toronto time, for 60 minutes: change the day, the time or the length with <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the page, or in Settings &gt; Program settings (Admin call). Every Admin gets the weekly calendar invite by email (a calendar file: accept it once and it repeats), and an update when the time changes. <b class="gd-ui">Add to my calendar (every week)</b> downloads the same event.</p><section class="gd-task" id="admin-call-the-deck" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The deck</h2><p class="gd-p">The deck builds itself the day before the call and again three hours before, from the live data; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> rebuilds it any time. An alert reaches the Admins an hour before. One slide a section:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Shifts for the coming week: what is published, the spots still open and each claim.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Staff hours (last 7 days) and the staff payouts owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Academy progress, person by person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Hiring: new applications, interviews booked, waiting for a decision, hired, and the interview no-shows by first name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Social media: the posts planned for the coming week, those still to approve, last week&#39;s posts and figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers of the last 7 days: bookings, revenue booked, occupancy, real visitors, conversion, leads by source and sales by rep.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owners: applications, cars onboarding, statements to approve, payouts due, cars in arrears.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to release or keep.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Insurance billing and replacement rentals.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Prepared money actions (from Claude).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet: cars out of service, maintenance To dos, cars free all next week, cars missing photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">To dos on the Admin queue that need a decision.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="admin-call-approve-and-deny" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve and Deny</h2><p class="gd-p">Every decision is on its slide with its two buttons, decided once (the name of the Admin who pressed it shows):</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><em>A shift claim</em>: Approve keeps it; Take off the shift removes the person from it.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">A To do</b>: Decline closes it with your reason; Approve leaves it open, marked approved.</li><li><em>A prepared money action</em>: Approve marks it approved and urgent; Decline closes it. No money moves from the deck: it moves only from its own screen.</li><li><em>A deposit</em> (Release or Keep) and <em>an owner payout</em> (Pay it or Hold it): the decision goes to Finance as a To do, done in Deposit reviews or Payouts with their usual checks.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Add a note to any slide. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens the call in the site, with the deck beside it; only Admins can join it.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'demo-portals', 'chapter', 'admin-call', null, 'Demo portals', 'A renter and an owner portal with made-up data.',
  'Team > Demo portals opens a **demo renter portal** and a **demo owner portal** with made-up data. Pick a stage at the top (Request sent to Closed for a renter; Application to Earning for an owner) to see what the customer sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and what they are sent. Every button only says what it would do: nothing is saved or sent. Every staff member has the same pages under Me > Academy > Demo portals, to learn each process.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Team &gt; Demo portals opens a <b class="gd-ui">demo renter portal</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">demo owner portal</b> with made-up data. Pick a stage at the top (Request sent to Closed for a renter; Application to Earning for an owner) to see what the customer sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and what they are sent. Every button only says what it would do: nothing is saved or sent. Every staff member has the same pages under Me &gt; Academy &gt; Demo portals, to learn each process.</p>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'chapter', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site''s own checks and published by themselves (the website''s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.

## The copy of a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.

1. The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car''s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.
2. Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what''s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.
3. To change a field press **Change**, then **Save and lock**. A locked field is kept by every new version. **Unlock** lets it be written again.
4. **Write again** asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car''s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.

> Good to know: The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car''s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.

## Landing pages and guides

**Settings**, then Search.

1. Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).
2. Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.
3. Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.
4. Open **Edit** on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. **Write again** asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.

## Vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...

1. Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.
2. One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: **Index the place pages**, **Index the colour pages**, **Index the search term pages**, **Index the /buy pages**, **Index the detailing pages**, **Index the body shop pages**. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.
3. The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.
4. **Oldest model year with vehicle pages** (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.
5. **Financing disclaimer**: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.
6. Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (the standard cap, 16,384 MB, by default: our own server''s disk; the small one, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.
7. Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.
8. Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People > Renters, the Leads tab.
9. Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.
10. Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. **Add trims for another model** adds a model that has none.
11. Catalog import: the last import and its counts. **Import now** asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.

> Good to know: A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car''s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.

## Stock photos on the vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: "Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons". The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.

1. Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet''s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked "not the exact year"; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.
2. The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.
3. Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press **Hide**. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.
4. **Pick again** asks for the next best photo; **Replace** takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.
5. **Show stock photos** in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).

> Good to know: Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer''s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.

## A car for sale

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car. On the For sale card, tick **For sale**, enter the Asking price and press **Save**.

1. The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.
2. Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.
3. "Find me this car" on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: **Owner leads**, Buyer leads), with a To do line.

## Search engines and business listings

**Settings**, then Site settings.

1. Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.
2. Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.
3. Business listings: press **Copy** beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.

> Good to know: Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.

## Place pages

Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. **Settings**, then Search.

1. Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.
2. Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.
3. Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.
4. Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.
5. Terms and services: change a term''s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for "price on request".
6. One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym''s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group''s page, which lists them ("Also searched as: ..."); only the group''s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.

> Good to know: A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.

## Alternative searches

People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting ("Turo Alternative in Mississauga"), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.

## Requests from the place pages

The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in **To do**: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.

Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as "Auto services we arrange": a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.

## One name, address and phone

The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.

## What search engines may read

**Settings**, **Vehicle pages**, **Search scope** says what search engines are invited to read:

- **Full (every page)**, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website''s CPU time as crawlers read them.
- **Core (about 23,000 pages)**: the fixed pages, the fleet''s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.

The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month''s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all ("try again tomorrow") until the month resets. People always get every page.

## IndexNow

**Search**, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.

### Index coverage

**Index coverage (Search Console sample)** shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.

### Longer pages from real data

Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR''s tolls, the city''s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car''s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.

> Good to know: After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on "Crawled - currently not indexed" (Indexing > Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.

### Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive

- **Positive pages**: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and **Request this exact car**; the checks refuse copy that says "not available", "we don''t have" or "we don''t offer".
- **Popular cars**: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says **Popular** with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.
- **Car figures**: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer''s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer''s colours, prices and equipment.
- **Parking**: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).
- **Events**: **Marketing** > **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.
- Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.
- **GPS tracker**: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).
- **Airports**: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.
- **Renting vs owning**: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.
- **Languages**: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).
- **Reviews**: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. **Reviews** > **Add a customer review** enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer''s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.
- Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page''s languages), each with its own dates.

> Good to know: The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.

## Search footprint and the clicks goal (releases 35 and 36)

- The search pages are in 18 languages spoken across the GTA, with page families for places, landing needs, cars and models, events, airports, comparisons with other rental companies and renting vs owning.
- Real reviews show on every car and search page, each with where it was received. Staff add a review that came by text, call, email or another platform exactly as received, with a screenshot.
- The SEO page in the Admin portal follows Search Console: clicks and impressions by week, pages indexed, and the progress to the goal of 5 million clicks, with the page families that bring the most.

## The tracker pages, every service on every page, and the new page design (release 48)

**The GPS tracker and kill switch** has its own pages now:

- `/trackers`: the product page, with the price (free for vehicle owners and for the first pre-orders, then the pre-order price, then the regular price after launch), the install and the monthly service by number of cars, what it does, a comparison table, questions and the form. `/gps-tracker` sends people there.
- `/trackers/kill-switch-for-car`, `starter-interrupt-device`, `gps-tracker-for-rental-car`, `anti-theft-tracker-toronto`, `fleet-tracking`, `turo-host-gps-tracker` and `toll-and-ticket-billing`: one page for each way people search.
- `/trackers/install` and `/trackers/install/` followed by the place: "tracker install near me", one page per Ontario place, with the same gate as the place pages.

Every price on those pages comes from **Settings** > **Program settings** (the tracker''s prices and the install price). While "Trackers can be installed" is off, every page says **Join the waitlist** with the words of "GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist" ("Shipping soon") and never says a tracker is in stock. Turn "Trackers can be installed" on when trackers can be installed: the same pages then take orders.

1. Someone joins the waitlist or pre-orders: a lead appears in **People** > **Renters** > **All leads** with the source "GPS tracker waitlist" or "GPS tracker pre-order", the number of cars and the price quoted, with its To do and the usual new-lead alert. The source ends with "(vehicle owner)" for an owner and "(free tracker)" for a free pre-order. The form has a box "My car is listed with CarmaCars (vehicle owner)": when the email is not an active owner''s, the lead says "check before the install", so confirm the person is an owner before the free tracker is promised.
2. The person gets a confirmation email that says how they joined (vehicle owner, pre-order or waitlist), what the tracker costs them, the install price and the monthly service for their number of cars. Nothing is charged.

**Every service on every page.** Each search page (landing pages, place pages, vehicle pages, the car page, events, airports) ends with the module **More from CarmaCars**: the tracker, List your car, chauffeur, delivery, coverage, monthly rentals, insurance replacement, rideshare, young drivers and the add-ons, each with its price when the database has one. `/services` lists every service with its pages.

**New landing pages**, edited like the others in **Settings** > **Search**: `rideshare`, `g2-licence`, `with-a-charger`, `with-flowers` and `with-child-seat`. The add-on pages show the add-on''s own price card from **Add-ons**, so change the price there, never in the copy.

**The page design.** Long pages are built from blocks: the short answer, the cars, price cards, the copy and the detail as folds (tap a heading to open it), questions, and on a phone a bar at the bottom with one button. The text is all still in the page for search engines.

> Good to know: a visitor who follows a Google, Bing, ChatGPT or Perplexity result to a place or vehicle page now gets the page at once. Before, a first visit could show "One moment, loading the page" for a second.
', 'Search: car pages, landing pages and guides', 'Car copy written by itself, landing pages, place pages for every place and term, detailing and body shop, guides, business listings and IndexNow.',
  'The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site''s own checks and published by themselves (the website''s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.

## The copy of a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.

1. The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car''s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.
2. Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what''s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.
3. To change a field press **Change**, then **Save and lock**. A locked field is kept by every new version. **Unlock** lets it be written again.
4. **Write again** asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car''s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.

> Good to know: The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car''s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.

## Landing pages and guides

**Settings**, then Search.

1. Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).
2. Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.
3. Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.
4. Open **Edit** on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. **Write again** asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.

## Vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...

1. Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.
2. One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: **Index the place pages**, **Index the colour pages**, **Index the search term pages**, **Index the /buy pages**, **Index the detailing pages**, **Index the body shop pages**. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.
3. The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.
4. **Oldest model year with vehicle pages** (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.
5. **Financing disclaimer**: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.
6. Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (the standard cap, 16,384 MB, by default: our own server''s disk; the small one, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.
7. Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.
8. Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People > Renters, the Leads tab.
9. Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.
10. Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. **Add trims for another model** adds a model that has none.
11. Catalog import: the last import and its counts. **Import now** asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.

> Good to know: A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car''s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.

## Stock photos on the vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: "Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons". The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.

1. Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet''s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked "not the exact year"; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.
2. The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.
3. Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press **Hide**. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.
4. **Pick again** asks for the next best photo; **Replace** takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.
5. **Show stock photos** in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).

> Good to know: Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer''s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.

## A car for sale

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car. On the For sale card, tick **For sale**, enter the Asking price and press **Save**.

1. The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.
2. Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.
3. "Find me this car" on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: **Owner leads**, Buyer leads), with a To do line.

## Search engines and business listings

**Settings**, then Site settings.

1. Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.
2. Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.
3. Business listings: press **Copy** beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.

> Good to know: Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.

## Place pages

Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. **Settings**, then Search.

1. Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.
2. Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.
3. Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.
4. Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.
5. Terms and services: change a term''s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for "price on request".
6. One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym''s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group''s page, which lists them ("Also searched as: ..."); only the group''s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.

> Good to know: A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.

## Alternative searches

People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting ("Turo Alternative in Mississauga"), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.

## Requests from the place pages

The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in **To do**: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.

Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as "Auto services we arrange": a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.

## One name, address and phone

The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.

## What search engines may read

**Settings**, **Vehicle pages**, **Search scope** says what search engines are invited to read:

- **Full (every page)**, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website''s CPU time as crawlers read them.
- **Core (about 23,000 pages)**: the fixed pages, the fleet''s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.

The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month''s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all ("try again tomorrow") until the month resets. People always get every page.

## IndexNow

**Search**, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.

### Index coverage

**Index coverage (Search Console sample)** shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.

### Longer pages from real data

Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR''s tolls, the city''s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car''s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.

> Good to know: After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on "Crawled - currently not indexed" (Indexing > Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.

### Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive

- **Positive pages**: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and **Request this exact car**; the checks refuse copy that says "not available", "we don''t have" or "we don''t offer".
- **Popular cars**: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says **Popular** with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.
- **Car figures**: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer''s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer''s colours, prices and equipment.
- **Parking**: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).
- **Events**: **Marketing** > **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.
- Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.
- **GPS tracker**: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).
- **Airports**: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.
- **Renting vs owning**: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.
- **Languages**: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).
- **Reviews**: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. **Reviews** > **Add a customer review** enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer''s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.
- Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page''s languages), each with its own dates.

> Good to know: The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.

