4. To add your number as a sign-in, use **Profile** > **Sign-in** > **Add and verify my phone number**. No code after a minute? Press **Resend the code**, or **Save it without a code**: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Customer service and Sales answer texts to the CarmaCars number in the same place as live chat. Every call and text is kept with the renter, owner or lead it belongs to.</p><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-answer-a-text" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a text</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> tab, and press <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>. Unread texts and missed calls are counted on each number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a number: calls and texts in order, and beside them who it is, with their bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the text and press <b class="gd-ui">Send text</b>. It goes from the CarmaCars number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Suggest a reply</b> writes a draft into the box. Read it and change it: it is never sent until you press Send text.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-unknown-callers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unknown callers</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Unknown callers</b>. Type the name if they told you and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> their name.</p><p class="gd-p">Quo&#39;s contacts follow the site: everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, added or updated within about five minutes. Change a name or number on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call gives you the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; when you have Live chat or Texts and calls open; otherwise it waits in the customer service queue. Call back with the Call button, or text, then mark the task done. Quo itself texts the caller back, so do not send the same message again.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A number that texted STOP gets no texts from us, booking texts included, until they text START. Prices go in a quote, never in a text from memory.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-email-text-or-both" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email, text or both</h2><p class="gd-p">Each renter and owner chooses how we reach them. Their page in Admin shows it under How we reach them; ask an Admin, or change it there if you can open the page. Texts need a phone they verified with a code. Your own choice is on your Profile, under Messages.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b> (customer service and Sales); press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin can switch the buttons back to the phone&#39;s own apps in Program settings. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every page of your portal (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (<b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a request, an offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>. It is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens their record. If it is outside your window, opening it from their call is logged as an opening for 24 hours with the reason Incoming call, as <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b> is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the line at the top right of the call to minimize it: it becomes a small chip at the bottom of the page with the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. Clicking anywhere outside the panel, or pressing Esc, minimizes it too. Press the chip to open the call again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. A new call always opens by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-through-the-site-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls through the site (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A call you place from the site (the Call button) opens the pop-up at once with the Call helper, for you only. It says <b class="gd-ui">Your call: on now</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Call ended</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the CarmaCars number that rings your browser opens the pop-up for you too. Sales get it now, not only customer service and Fleet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every call through the site is recorded, turned into text and summarised. Open the renter and choose <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> in the Activity log: press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Show the transcript</b> on a call.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Inside every call on the pop-up, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> tells you what to say and do. It is made for your first weeks; press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> when you no longer need it (<b class="gd-ui">Show</b> brings it back).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Say</b>: the greeting to read out, with your first name, and the caller&#39;s name and booking when we know them. Start every call with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What is the call about?</b> Press the button that fits: New booking or price question, Change or extend a booking, Running late or late return, Pick-up and delivery, Deposit and payments, Insurance and protection, Accident or damage, Complaint, Owner wants to list a car, or Job applicant. You get 3 to 6 short steps. Words in bold quotes are what to say; a link opens the right page of your portal. <b class="gd-ui">All situations</b> goes back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>: type a word (deposit, late, cancel, km) for the short answer to the questions callers ask most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts, days and percentages in the steps and answers come from the settings, so they are always the ones in force. Never quote a price from memory: the offer screen works it out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Always finish with <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin writes the greetings, the steps and the answers. Something wrong or missing? Tell an Admin: they change it in Settings and you see it on the next call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s record (<b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>, then Open) has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and the notes are in its Activity log (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>), newest first, each with the date and time, who wrote it and their role. Add a note for every situation: what they asked, what you told them, what happens next. Notes cannot be changed or removed by staff, so write a new note to correct one; an Admin can remove a note with a reason. The notes also show on the caller pop-up and on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-lanes-the-call-button-and-hidden-numbers-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lanes, the Call button and hidden numbers (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each conversation has a lane: <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> for a car on rent, or a pickup, return, delivery or collection within a day; <b class="gd-ui">Customer service</b> for the rest. The inbox has a tab for each. The caller pop-up rings for Fleet first on Fleet&#39;s calls; customer service gets them when no Fleet staff member is on duty or nobody answered within 20 seconds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> places the call in your browser (release 44, below): the customer sees the CarmaCars number, and the call is noted on their history with its length. Until calling from the site is set up, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo as before and says why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-in-your-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in your browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">You make and take calls in the staff portal, in your browser, on the CarmaCars number. Your own phone number is never used and never shown, wherever you work from.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Use a computer with a headset (or earphones with a microphone) in Chrome, Edge or Safari. The first time you call, the browser asks to use the microphone: press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a booking or any staff page. The call screen opens (a card at the bottom left on a computer, the whole screen on a phone) with the person&#39;s name, the number and <b class="gd-ui">Starting the call...</b>, then the call&#39;s timer once they answer. The customer sees the CarmaCars number. Sales: the number stays hidden, the call goes through all the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To call someone without opening their page, press the round green phone button at the bottom left. <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b>: type any number and press the green button. <b class="gd-ui">Contacts</b>: the people you called last, or type a name or number to find a lead (Sales: your own leads) or a renter, then tap the person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">During the call: <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> (for a phone menu that asks you to press a number), <b class="gd-ui">Speaker</b> (choose the microphone and, where the browser allows, the speaker), <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> and the red <b class="gd-ui">End call</b> button. <b class="gd-ui">End call</b> is always on the screen, also while the call is still starting (it then says <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>). Switching apps on a phone keeps the call on; closing the page ends a call that is still starting.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Incoming calls: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, your browser rings while a staff page is open (customer service and Sales by default). Press <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. The first person to answer takes the call and the others stop ringing. You see the caller&#39;s name when we know it (Sales: the number hidden).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online, or nobody answers: the caller hears a short message, and it is a missed call with its task, like every missed call. A call is never forwarded to your own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Keep a staff page open during your shift with the computer&#39;s sound on, so you hear the ring.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A call that fails (the microphone not allowed, the connection lost): the call screen says what to do. Press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>, fix it and call again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calling-from-the-site-your-mobile-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calling from the site: your mobile (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a request or a booking rings your own mobile first, then connects the person. They see the CarmaCars number, never yours. Sales see the number hidden and call this way only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The first time, with no mobile on your profile, a small window asks <b class="gd-ui">Your mobile number</b>. Type your Canadian or US mobile (10 digits, for example (647) 555-0123) and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and call</b>. No code is texted: it is saved to your profile and the call starts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your phone rings. Answer it: you hear &quot;CarmaCars call. Connecting you now.&quot; and the person&#39;s phone rings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A call that cannot start says why in the same window, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>. Calling from the site not set up: ask customer service or an Admin to call, and tell an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To add your number as a sign-in, use <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sign-in</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>. No code after a minute? Press <b class="gd-ui">Resend the code</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Save it without a code</b>: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'car-maintenance', 'chapter', 'assistant', 'Fleet keeps every car serviced: oil, tires, brakes, inspections and the registration. Finance bills what Fleet records. Recording a service resets its reminders and makes its bill.

## What is due

Open **Field work** > **Maintenance** (Finance: **Money** > **Maintenance bills**).

1. Every car, most urgent first: overdue (red), due soon, no record yet (dashed), all OK.
2. Your To do has one Service due task per car listing what is due. Open it: the car opens with the record pop-up.
3. A car with no record yet has one task to record its last service. Enter what you know once.

## Record a service

1. Press **Record a service** on the car (or **Record** on one item of the car''s Maintenance).
2. Tick what was done, check the date and the odometer, type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST, and add the receipt.
3. Who pays: the owner for an owner''s car (deducted on their statement), CarmaCars for a company car, a claim, the renter, or no charge.
4. Leave **The bill is in: bill it now** ticked, or untick it and press **Bill now** on the record later.
5. Press **Record the service**. The items done are OK again.

> Watch out: Above your single limit the service is recorded and the timers reset, but an Admin bills it: you see "An Admin bills it".

## Tires, swaps and readings

- Under Tires: **Add a tire set** (kind, size, brand, tread, made and bought dates, where it is stored), **Put on the car** to swap.
- Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1. Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread, overdue at 3 mm.
- **Add a reading** when you see the odometer. Handover, return and move readings come in by themselves.
- A car whose recorded safety inspection or registration has expired cannot be handed over until the renewal is recorded.
', 'Car maintenance', 'The maintenance list, recording a service in one step, tires and swaps, readings, and billing.',
  'Fleet keeps every car serviced: oil, tires, brakes, inspections and the registration. Finance bills what Fleet records. Recording a service resets its reminders and makes its bill.

## What is due

Open **Field work** > **Maintenance** (Finance: **More finance** > **Maintenance and expenses**).

1. Every car, most urgent first: overdue (red), due soon, no record yet (dashed), all OK.
2. Your To do has one Service due task per car listing what is due. Open it: the car opens with the record pop-up.
3. A car with no record yet has one task to record its last service. Enter what you know once.

## Record a service

1. Press **Record a service** on the car (or **Record** on one item of the car''s Maintenance).
2. Tick what was done, check the date and the odometer, type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST, and add the receipt.
3. Who pays: the owner for an owner''s car (deducted on their statement), CarmaCars for a company car, a claim, the renter, or no charge.
4. Leave **The bill is in: bill it now** ticked, or untick it and press **Bill now** on the record later.
5. Press **Record the service**. The items done are OK again.

> Watch out: Above your single limit the service is recorded and the timers reset, but an Admin bills it: you see "An Admin bills it".

## Tires, swaps and readings

- Under Tires: **Add a tire set** (kind, size, brand, tread, made and bought dates, where it is stored), **Put on the car** to swap.
- Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1. Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread, overdue at 3 mm.
- **Add a reading** when you see the odometer. Handover, return and move readings come in by themselves.
- A car whose recorded safety inspection or registration has expired cannot be handed over until the renewal is recorded.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Fleet keeps every car serviced: oil, tires, brakes, inspections and the registration. Finance bills what Fleet records. Recording a service resets its reminders and makes its bill.</p><section class="gd-task" id="car-maintenance-what-is-due" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What is due</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Field work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> (Finance: <b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance and expenses</b>).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car, most urgent first: overdue (red), due soon, no record yet (dashed), all OK.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your To do has one Service due task per car listing what is due. Open it: the car opens with the record pop-up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no record yet has one task to record its last service. Enter what you know once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="car-maintenance-record-a-service" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Record a service</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a service</b> on the car (or <b class="gd-ui">Record</b> on one item of the car&#39;s Maintenance).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick what was done, check the date and the odometer, type the shop, the cost before HST and the HST, and add the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the owner for an owner&#39;s car (deducted on their statement), CarmaCars for a company car, a claim, the renter, or no charge.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leave <b class="gd-ui">The bill is in: bill it now</b> ticked, or untick it and press <b class="gd-ui">Bill now</b> on the record later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the service</b>. The items done are OK again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Above your single limit the service is recorded and the timers reset, but an Admin bills it: you see &quot;An Admin bills it&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="car-maintenance-tires-swaps-and-readings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tires, swaps and readings</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Under Tires: <b class="gd-ui">Add a tire set</b> (kind, size, brand, tread, made and bought dates, where it is stored), <b class="gd-ui">Put on the car</b> to swap.</li><li>Ontario: winter tires on by December 1 (reminder from November 1), off after April 1. Tires are due soon at 4 mm of tread, overdue at 3 mm.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Add a reading</b> when you see the odometer. Handover, return and move readings come in by themselves.</li><li>A car whose recorded safety inspection or registration has expired cannot be handed over until the renewal is recorded.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'demo-portals', 'chapter', 'shared-tools', null, 'Demo portals and the game in Rewards', 'See each process as a customer does; play for points.',
  'Me > Academy > **Demo portals** opens a demo renter portal and a demo owner portal with made-up data. Pick a stage to see exactly what the renter or the owner sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and the emails and texts they get. Nothing you press there is saved or sent, so use it to learn each process or to walk a customer through theirs on the phone.

On a booking''s Overview, **From sale to pickup** shows the steps to close the sale and get the customer ready: request answered, offer accepted, agreement signed, paid, licence and coverage checked, deposit and drivers, car prepared, picked up. The step to do now is marked, with **Go there**; a step that waits on the renter says so, so you know to nudge them.

## The game in Rewards

Rewards has **Today''s game**: press **Play now** and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go to your own Rewards account (as a renter); if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Me &gt; Academy &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Demo portals</b> opens a demo renter portal and a demo owner portal with made-up data. Pick a stage to see exactly what the renter or the owner sees then: the next step, the countdown to pickup, the step tracker, the money and the emails and texts they get. Nothing you press there is saved or sent, so use it to learn each process or to walk a customer through theirs on the phone.</p><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Overview, <b class="gd-ui">From sale to pickup</b> shows the steps to close the sale and get the customer ready: request answered, offer accepted, agreement signed, paid, licence and coverage checked, deposit and drivers, car prepared, picked up. The step to do now is marked, with <b class="gd-ui">Go there</b>; a step that waits on the renter says so, so you know to nudge them.</p><section class="gd-task" id="demo-portals-the-game-in-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The game in Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Rewards has <b class="gd-ui">Today&#39;s game</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Play now</b> and one of the discount games (the wheel, a scratch card, blackjack and the others) shows your prize. Every game wins CarmaCars Rewards points, never a discount code: 10 to 250 points, drawn by the site, not by the game. One game a day (Admins set how many). Your points go to your own Rewards account (as a renter); if you have never rented with us they are saved and move there by themselves when you do. Points are never cash: they come off a rental charge only, from 500 points, like every other Rewards point. A test account plays but earns nothing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.


### Your shifts in Google Calendar

On **My shifts** (and on **Profile**), **Add my shifts and townhalls to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with the shifts you claimed, the tasks given to you and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. New and changed shifts show by themselves; Google refreshes every few hours. Keep the link to yourself: **Regenerate link** stops the old one.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.

## Your tips

**My pay** shows **My tips**: your half of each tip on a car you handed over (all of it when you also sold the rental). A tip given to you in cash: tell the office, they record it on the booking''s Money tab.
